# the ring is sealed

The ring lives in the `MuseoKit` Swift package (GitHub `its4ff/museo-kit`, pinned to an exact version; `scripts/local-kit.sh` swaps in a local `../museo-kit` for kit work). Never copy its files into this repo, edit it from here, or wrap or replace `RingBLEManager`. This repo has no CoreBluetooth, GATT, Treaty frames, raw BLE or second bluetooth stack.

```swift
// BAD: a second bluetooth stack, raw protocol, or anything copied out of the kit
let central = CBCentralManager(delegate: self, queue: nil)
peripheral.writeValue(frame, for: tx, type: .withoutResponse)

// GOOD: read the ring's status in a view, react to muses and ring events in your code
struct RingLine: View {
    @Environment(RingModel.self) private var ring
    var body: some View {
        Text(ring.status.shortLine)              // "ring linked", "listening…", "bringing in 3"
            .font(MuseType.body)
            .foregroundStyle(MuseColor.ink70)
    }
}
// App/YourCode.swift
MuseHooks.onTranscribed { muse in print("[muse][yours]", muse.words) }
Museo.onEvent { event in if case .liveStarted = event { MuseHaptics.play(.soft) } }
```

- `Museo.start(name:clearsRingAfterSync:)` runs once, in `App/AppStart.swift`, from the app delegate. Never in a view.
- Finished recordings come through `Museo.onCapture`, and only `MusePipeline` uses it. It saves the muse and flushes to disk before returning true; only then does the kit let the ring retire its copy. Keep that order.
- Ring events: `Museo.onEvent { }` or `Museo.events()`, any number of listeners. Never set the manager's `on…` callbacks.
- Views read `RingModel.status` (`RingStatus`). Ring buttons go through `RingActions`. Firmware through `Museo.firmware`. `Museo.manager` is for low-level tools like the ring console, never screens.
- Only a confirmed tap may clear the ring. One ring app per phone. Recording is always 24 kbps, with no setting.
- If a task needs the ring's protocol, it's a kit change: say so and stop.

Build in `App/YourCode.swift`, `Screens/` and `Design/`. AGENTS.md has the map. Ring screens: the `museo-ring` skill.
